      "sourceTextSha256": "0293a55346979c5fe4f0b3178b9435e65146daccf54f4630766631d2a04a7aff",
      "text": "Begin your journey in Buenos Aires, discovering the elegance and vibrant culture of Argentina’s capital, before heading south to the glaciers and dramatic landscapes of El Calafate. Continue to Ushuaia, often called the southernmost city in the world, surrounded by the wild beauty of Tierra del Fuego, and finally travel north to the spectacular Iguazú Falls, where the journey ends among rainforest and rushing waters.\n\nDay 3 · Breakfast at the hotel. Free day for optional tours: Tigre and the Northern Zone, a Fiesta Gaucha at the Santa Susana ranch or a day trip to Colonia del Sacramento, Uruguay (see Optional Excursions).\n\n## Hotels and prices\n\nAccommodation: 474 Buenos Aires — 4 nights, Calafate Parque — 2 nights, Wyndham Garden Ushuaia — 2 nights, Mercure Iguazu — 3 nights.\n\n| Travellers | Room type | Price per person |\n|---|---|---:|\n| 1 guest | SGL | $7 568 |\n| 2 guests | SGL | $5 651 |\n| 2 guests | DBL | $4 036 |\n| 3 guests | SGL | $5 265 |\n| 3 guests | DBL | $3 650 |\n| 3 guests | TRL | $3 578 |\n\n",
